Option 1 (simplest for single-Nginx setup): trust only X-Real-IP set by Nginx (which Nginx sets to $remote_addr, not forwarded verbatim):

def _get_client_ip(request) -> str:
    real_ip = request.META.get('HTTP_X_REAL_IP')
    if real_ip:
        return real_ip.strip()
    return request.META.get('REMOTE_ADDR', '0.0.0.0')

Option 2: take the rightmost value from XFF (xff.split(',')[-1].strip()), which is the last hop appended by your own trusted proxy and is not spoofable by the client. Add NUM_PROXIES = 1 to REST_FRAMEWORK settings for DRF throttle consistency.

